icy durable through a normal exact-revision review request. Scope only agents/builder/agent.md and agents/fixer/agent.md (or their established shared owner if current primary already centralizes this policy). Build from current origin primary; do not copy dirty main-checkout files wholesale or import unrelated operational edits.\\n\\nBefore preparing review-request payloads, both roles must fetch origin and require the final checked revision to contain origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}. If stale, rebase their subject/repair onto the fetched primary, preserve both feature and primary behavior, and rerun every configured check before publishing the resulting SHA. Failed rebase/check stops publication. Fixer must retain the original rejected SHA for Kernel compare-and-swap. Preserve Kernel atomic publication and the Verifier/Gate ancestry check: this guard reduces avoidable stale publication but cannot eliminate later races. Add no scheduler, retry loop, dependency, new role, or Kernel code.\\n\\nEvidence: collision revision 34b04b06de58ebfe735dedd977b00c2a614cc752 passed checks but was stale because 73d1489 landed during implementation. Local Fixer policy digest 4d7e25ef73d3dad94e08d461a7347a6c4cde500e195c81bd3d60d4c547671c32 was exercised by Run 1788552644310643252-fixer: it refetched, verified ancestry, and published 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 with original rejected-SHA CAS.\\n\\nAcceptance: reviewable minimal role-policy diff on current primary; supported forest declaration show loads both declarations without errors; repository checks pass; exact request/verdict/Gate evidence integrates the policy. Do not add source-text tests for prompts or claim local runtime hashes prove Git integration.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:17:54.108Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-