ct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:39:32.665Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:56:11.467Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\nEXIT:0\n=== ls-remote mine ===\n3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267\trefs/heads/forest/canopy-critic-discovery-id-collision/discovery-id-collision\n=== ls-remote takeable ===\n=== github ready ===\nEXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788553266070}}
