d-swap. Preserve Kernel atomic publication and the Verifier/Gate ancestry check: this guard reduces avoidable stale publication but cannot eliminate later races. Add no scheduler, retry loop, dependency, new role, or Kernel code.\\n\\nEvidence: collision revision 34b04b06de58ebfe735dedd977b00c2a614cc752 passed checks but was stale because 73d1489 landed during implementation. Local Fixer policy digest 4d7e25ef73d3dad94e08d461a7347a6c4cde500e195c81bd3d60d4c547671c32 was exercised by Run 1788552644310643252-fixer: it refetched, verified ancestry, and published 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 with original rejected-SHA CAS.\\n\\nAcceptance: reviewable minimal role-policy diff on current primary; supported forest declaration show loads both declarations without errors; repository checks pass; exact request/verdict/Gate evidence integrates the policy. Do not add source-text tests for prompts or claim local runtime hashes prove Git integration.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:16:08.947Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:17:54.108Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": false,\n    \"takeable\": true\n  }\n}\n===BRANCH CHECK DONE===\nREMOTE_EMPTY_EXIT:0\nPR_EXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788553288084}}
